=== xrandr
--- xrandr --output 
DP-1 	connected
HDMI-1 	disconnected
eDP-1 	connected
--- xrandr --output DP-1 --mode 
1280x720 	60.00
1920x1080 	60.00    50.00
2560x1440 	59.95*+
--- xrandr --output eDP-1 --mode 1920x1080 --output DP-1 --right-of 
DP-1 	connected
HDMI-1 	disconnected
eDP-1 	connected
--- xrandr --rot
--rotate 	rotate the output
--- xrandr --output DP-1 --rotate 
inverted 
left 
normal 
right 
--- xrandr -d :1 --output 
DP-1 	connected
HDMI-1 	disconnected
eDP-1 	connected
--- xrandr --mode 
1280x720 	60.00    59.99
1680x1050 	59.95
1920x1080 	60.01*+  59.97    59.96
2560x1440 	59.95*+
=== gsettings
--- gsettings 
describe 	show the description of a key
get 	get the value of a key
help 	show the help (of a command)
list-children 	list the children of a schema
list-keys 	list the keys of a schema
list-recursively 	list the keys and values, recursively
list-relocatable-schemas 	list the relocatable schemas
list-schemas 	list the installed schemas
monitor 	watch for changes
range 	show the range of a key's values
reset 	reset a key to its default
reset-recursively 	reset all the keys of a schema
set 	set the value of a key
writable 	check whether a key is writable
--- gsettings g
get 	get the value of a key
--- gsettings get 
org.gnome.desktop.interface 
org.gnome.desktop.wm.preferences 
--- gsettings get org.gnome.desktop.interface 
clock-show-seconds 
color-scheme 
text-scaling-factor 
--- gsettings --schemadir dir set org.gnome.desktop.interface color-scheme 
default 
prefer-dark 
prefer-light 
--- gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.interface clock-show-seconds 
false 
true 
--- gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.interface text-scaling-factor 
--- gsettings list-keys org.gnome.desktop.wm.preferences 
--- gsettings list-schemas --
--print-paths 	show the paths of the schemas
--- gsettings help r
range 
reset 
reset-recursively 
=== dconf
--- dconf 
compile 	compile a binary database from key files
dump 	dump a directory to standard output
help 	show the help (of a command)
list 	list the contents of a directory
load 	load a directory from standard input
read 	read the value of a key
reset 	reset a key or directory
update 	update the system databases
watch 	watch a path for changes
write 	write the value of a key
